MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Heat shrink tubing fits my electronics projects because it would insulate the wiring connecting battery holders, relays, and other components.",
    "Alligator clips and screw terminals support the same hands-on work as my breadboards and PCB supplies: making temporary test connections or securing wiring that I may need to adjust. The clips would be useful if they fit my existing leads."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The smaller nylon casters miss the specific features of my recent choice: larger heavy-duty wheels with levelers. Having bought casters does not mean another set would meet the same need.",
    "An infrared thermometer helps me check temperatures, but that does not establish a need for automated heating and cooling. Likewise, adhesives, plumbing tape, nails, and pegboard hooks need specific projects that I have not indicated."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics and occasional DIY seems to have been stretched into a general need for workshop and repair supplies.",
    "Shared functions such as temperature-related work or furniture mobility seem to count too much when the actual task and required features differ."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my purchases involve assembling and wiring small electronic circuits, so supplies that help connect, test, and insulate those circuits have a clear practical use for me.",
    "I choose moderately and need a concrete reason to add something. A recent equipment purchase may already cover that need, while a specialized repair product is hard to justify without a matching repair."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my electronics work but extended that interest too broadly into unrelated repairs and equipment needs."
}
